# Child repos, cloned by `repo sync`. Each keeps its own history in its own remote; this repo
# tracks only the `default.xml` manifest and the conventions beside it.
#
# `repo init` puts the manifest in `.repo/manifests` and the children beside it, so a workspace
# rooted on this checkout is the case these patterns are for. Every entry in `default.xml` must
# be matched here, or its clone appears as untracked and the next person to run `git status` is
# invited to commit somebody else's repository into this one. Checked with:
#
#   python3 -c "import xml.etree.ElementTree as E,subprocess; [print('MISSING',d) for d in (p.get('path') or p.get('name') for p in E.parse('default.xml').getroot().iter('project')) if subprocess.run(['git','check-ignore','-q',d+'/']).returncode]"
#
# The trailing slash is the whole check. Every pattern below ends in one, so `check-ignore`
# matches only a path it can see is a directory. Without it the command reports MISSING for
# every child not yet cloned, which is the state a fresh checkout is in and the state this
# check is most wanted in.
#
# `default.xml` gives each child a `path`, so a child lands in the directory for its side of
# the hexagon and one entry covers that whole side. A child added to a side later is ignored
# without an edit here. Six entries is the whole list, because every project sits on a side;
# the eight directories that used to be named here one by one named how a thing was built or
# where it came from, and each was a place for whatever nobody had classified.
/1-transport/
/2-contract/
/3-interactor/
/4-entities/
/5-repository/
/6-datasource/
# Neither 7 nor 0 is a side. A service packs sides into one deployable thing, so it sits past
# the ring rather than on it. 0 holds the fabric's record of itself, which is a subject of no
# side because every side is a subject of it; it is where this repository's CLAUDE.md, ledger,
# checks and logbook went when the manifest stopped carrying them.
/7-service/
/0-infrastructure/

# Build and run output from work done at the workspace root rather than inside a child. Logs
# from a long engine build or a test server land here and are worth keeping on disk while a
# session runs, and worth keeping out of a manifest repository afterwards.
*.log

# Scratch that is neither a child repo nor a build artefact.
.repo/
node_modules/
/.playwright-mcp/

# Built from memory/*.usda by misc/scripts/memory.py; the relations are the source.
/memory/fabric.sqlite3
/.DS_Store

# The doc gate is a mix application. Its build output, its fetched dependency and its
# dialyzer PLTs are all derived from mix.exs and mix.lock, so none of them is tracked.
misc/checks/_build/
misc/checks/deps/
misc/checks/priv/plts/
